Description:
As a Quantitative Analyst, you will support power price and production forecast unit for math, optimization and in-depth data related tasks.

In this role, you will:


develop, maintain and continuously improve core forecasting, simulation and decision support solutions;
design and implement tools for forecasting, and operational planning;
contribute to quantitative models, algorithmic solutions, data processing workflows, and system automation initiatives across multiple business domains;
handle and process weather-related datasets, including gridded data sources;
integrate weather-related models and data streams into systems;
develop and maintain renewable asset forecasting solutions at both the individual asset and portfolio levels;
prepare, update, and maintain technical documentation and presentation materials;
validate and backtest models, identify improvement opportunities, and collaborate with data engineers to implement enhancements;
contribute to cross-functional projects and other ad hoc data, modelling, and analytics initiatives.


With us, you can:


develop professionally through continuous training and development programs that expand your skills and experience;
opportunity for long-term career growth and self-fulfillment in a growing international company;
enjoy 5 additional vacation days after your first year;
choose a well‑being package that suits you, including health insurance and/or Stebby services.


You are a great match if you:


have work experience in the fields of Data Analysis, Data Science, or Quantitative Analysis;
have strong analytical and data-related skills, including developing complex prediction models, solving optimization problems, automating, and handling large volumes of data;
are experienced in either R or Python, complemented by a basic familiarity with the other;
are familiar with data workflows, including data storage, access, and transformation (SQL, data import/export, and Parquet files);
are a results-oriented team player with an eagerness to learn;
hold a university degree in Mathematics, Statistics, Data Science, or a related field;
speak fluent English.


Additional Details

Location: Tallinn. Partial remote work opportunity.

Apply latest by 10.09.2026.
Show more

We’re a team of 500+ professionals who develop cutting-edge proxy and web data scraping solutions for thousands of the world’s best known businesses, including Fortune 500 companies.

What’s in store for you:

You’ll be developing complex products with high coding standards, maintaining our own infrastructure, handling petabytes of data, and solving challenges on a daily basis. We got you covered with a team of strong professionals to support you, a well-built tech stack, and loads of ownership.

The Data Analytics team empowers our entire organization by transforming complex data into actionable business insights and building robust self-service tools. As a Data Analyst, you will play a crucial role in modeling customer behavior and marketing data to directly support senior stakeholders and commercial teams.

In this role, you will:


Develop a foundational understanding of the relationships between customer behavior and our growth drivers through data analysis and data modelling;
Assist in creating and maintaining self-service dashboards for stakeholders across the business, using PowerBI or Superset;
Model and connect marketing campaign, channel, and touchpoint data to help us better understand the customer journey from acquisition to conversion;
Utilize analytical tools (SQL, Python, Google Sheets) to prepare and analyze data, supporting key decision-making processes;
Leverage AI tools to accelerate data analysis workflows and improve productivity;
Identify new research areas that should be pursued and provide recommendations to senior stakeholders;
Conduct ad-hoc analysis to address stakeholder questions, focusing on commercial impact and effectively communicating your findings



Your skills & experiences:


2+ years of experience working closely with business leaders in an analytical or consulting role, driving measurable business impact;
Strong proficiency in SQL for data manipulation, alongside experience with visualization tools (PowerBI, Superset, Tableau, Looker) and Excel/Google Sheets;
Understanding of when and how to leverage AI in both analytical and business workflows;
A pragmatic, problem-solving mindset—you know when a quick Excel pivot beats a complex Python script, and you view AI as a valuable productivity multiplier
Excellent English communication skills, allowing you to clearly translate technical findings and comfortably engage in engineering-related discussions



Nice to have:


Solid understanding of marketing metrics (funnel, cohort, and campaign analysis), ideally combined with SaaS metrics (MRR, LTV/CAC), and a strong commercial awareness focused on user needs



Tech Stack:


Google Cloud Platform (GCS, BQ) for storage and warehousing;
dbt and SQL for data modelling;
Python for automation;
Jupyter for ad-hoc analysis;
PowerBI and Superset for data visualisation;
Airflow for orchestration



Salary & Benefits:


Gross salary: 3200-4500 EUR/month. Keep in mind that we are open to discuss a different salary based on your skills and competencies
Growth & Learning: 40+ internal learning options, external conferences, mentorship, and year-round knowledge-sharing
Health & Well-being: Private health insurance, psychotherapy, on-site well-being consultants, 24/7 gym access, and a wellness app
Celebration & Community: Team events, an overseas workation, quarterly team-building budgets, and plenty of ways to mark milestones together
Plus bonus vacation days, paid life-moment days off, barista coffee, and all the tools you need. See the full list of benefits here: https://career.oxylabs.io/blog/our-work-benefits/



Up for the challenge? Let’s talk!

We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.
